<title>UK: Amec says plans sales of Egypt Gas stake.</title>
<headline>Amec says plans sales of Egypt Gas stake.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON</dateline>
<text>
<p>British engineering and construction group Amec Plc said on Thursday it was well-advanced in talks to sell its 20 percent stake in Egypt Gas through an institution placing.</p>
<p>In a statement it explained that the plan would be to sell the shares for a gross cash consideration of 38.1 million stg, giving it a profit on disposal of about 30 million stg, subject to tax.</p>
<p>Amec bought its Egypt Gas stake when the company was formed in 1983 to maintain and develop a gas distribution system installed by Amec in Cairo.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
